 "do_bench_offset_us": {
  "value": 25.806000000000004,
  "source": "host_overhead.py on the 1024^3 pick: TileLang do_bench event median 73.6 us against 47.8 us wall-clock per call back-to-back and 45.1 us in the ablation harness; cuTensorMapEncodeTiled is 0.47 us",
  "note": "every sweep, sample and baseline timing taken through do_bench carries this per-call offset; the harness and cuBLASLt's harness do not",
  "mechanism": "tilelang/profiler/bench.py: do_bench writes a 256 MB flush buffer between timed calls (fast_flush, cache_size=256). The timed kernel then starts with a cold L2 (A and B come from DRAM: 6.3 MB / 235 GB/s = 27 us at 1024^3) and with dirty lines draining to DRAM (up to 24 MB). The offset is per call, not per launch, and it is largest where the kernel is short or DRAM-bound. The ablation harness and the cuBLASLt harness time back-to-back launches with a warm L2; the two conditions are both real, and they must not be mixed."
 },
